===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|bouquet garni|lit=garnished bouquet}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|bouquets garnis|nolinkhead=1}}

# A bundled mixture of [[herb]]s or dried [[herb]]s used as a flavouring for [[stew]]s, [[soup]]s{{,}} and [[sauce]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Ruth Lively|title=Cooking from the Garden|publisher=Taunton Press|isbn=9781600852473|page=117
|passage=In the past, the '''bouquet garni''' was a prescribed mixture of thyme, bay leaf, and parsley. But thankfully the traditional formula has changed as cooking methods have become less regimented.}}

